Let $M$ be a closed (compact, without boundary) smooth manifold of dimension at least $2$, and for an integer $k \geq 2$ let $\mathcal{G}^{k}(M)$ denote the space of smooth Riemannian metrics on $M$ equipped with the $C^{k}$-topology. For a metric $g \in \mathcal{G}^{k}(M)$, let $\varphi^{g}_{t}$ denote its geodesic flow on the unit tangent bundle $SM$, and let $h_{\mathrm{top}}(\varphi^{g})$ denote its topological entropy.

Determine whether each of the following sets is dense in $\mathcal{G}^{k}(M)$:

(i) the set of metrics $g$ for which $h_{\mathrm{top}}(\varphi^{g}) > 0$;

(ii) (assuming $\dim M \geq 3$) the set of metrics $g$ for which the geodesic flow $\varphi^{g}$ is transitive, i.e. there exists an orbit whose closure is all of $SM$;

(iii) the set of metrics $g$ for which the union of tangent vectors to closed geodesics is dense in $SM$.

